{
  "_comment": "Copy this file to urtc_config.json. Only 'language' is needed. Add 'hmac_key_hex' / 'slave_hmac_key_hex' (64 hexadecimal digits) ONLY to flash an image you built yourself with that key; the other fields are compiled-in values and should be left out. Set 'require_production_signature' to true to refuse images signed with the public development key (the bundled official images are). Every update report is signed with a key of your own that is made on first use (~/.urtc-keys/records_ed25519.key, or the file named by URTC_RECORD_KEY_FILE); set 'sign_update_reports' to false to write it unsigned. 'image_header_policy' says what to do with an image that has no header inside it: 'accept', 'warn' (the default) or 'require'; a header that is there is always checked. 'optional_functions_panel' (false unless it is exactly true) shows a panel in the CAN-OTA window with a check box for the emergency stop following of a tool head and a button that writes it; a flash never writes it.",
  "language": "english"
}
